/-!
# Input isometries from the original corrected sources

The endpoint Schmidt matrices at the original source occurrences determine the
proper tensor frame of the corrected registers. The original occurrence index
is retained, independently of the partial branch and of the numerical source
vectors. Exact crossing sources supply the remaining two Schmidt frames.

Source: polynomial-PEPS Theorem 5.2, `04-compression.tex`, lines 383–434.
-/

